* Disable a model.
* Disable a prompt version.
* Suspend a tool.
* Disable one AI-powered feature.
* Switch to a verified fallback.
* Require manual processing.
* Restrict usage by budget or quota.

Every circuit-breaker action must be authorized and audited.

A global AI shutdown must not unnecessarily disable unrelated non-AI platform functions.

