2.55 Mandatory Git Workflow

The control center must reflect this working model:

1. No direct work on the protected main branch.
2. Contributor obtains the latest approved main branch.
3. Contributor creates a dedicated feature branch.
4. Contributor works only within the assigned scope.
5. Contributor runs relevant tests.
6. Contributor records changed, added, moved, and deleted files.
7. Contributor commits changes.
8. Contributor pushes to the dedicated branch.
9. Contributor opens a pull request.
10. Independent review takes place.
11. Required checks pass.
12. Conflicts and integration risks are resolved.
13. Authorized merge occurs.
14. Post-merge verification takes place.

Pushing a branch is not approval.

Opening a pull request is not approval.

Passing tests does not automatically establish that a change is safe.

